@@ -93,6 +94,16 @@ The TCK supports three A2A transports:
 
 Transport selection is driven by the agent card's `supportedInterfaces`. The TCK fetches the agent card from `{sut-host}/.well-known/agent-card.json` and creates clients for each declared interface. Use `--transport` to filter which transports are tested.
 
+For an agent requiring HTTP authentication, supply an importable
+`--http-auth-provider module:factory`. The factory receives keyword arguments
+`transport` (`jsonrpc` or `http_json`) and `agent_card` (the discovered card),
+and must return an `httpx.Auth` instance. The implementor owns credentials and
+any extension-specific request signing. The same authenticated session carries
+normal operations, streaming, and raw probes that customize headers or send
+invalid input; protocol assertions and response bodies remain unchanged.
+Provider errors fail the run instead of retrying anonymously. Public card
+discovery remains unauthenticated; this option does not configure gRPC auth.
+
 ## Reports
 
 Reports are always generated in the `reports/` directory after every run:
@@ -104,6 +115,14 @@ Reports are always generated in the `reports/` directory after every run:
 | pytest HTML | `reports/tck_report.html` | Standard pytest-html report |
 | JUnit XML | `reports/junitreport.xml` | JUnit XML for CI integration |
 
+Scores describe **automated checks**. Requirements tagged `not-automatable`
+(such as signed-card verification and client tenant propagation) appear as
+`MANUAL`, with a pending-verification list in console, HTML and JSON reports.
+They are excluded from automated percentages and never count as passes.
+`NOT TESTED` automated requirements still lower the score, including when the
+SUT was unreachable. A 100% automated score does not establish full conformance
+while manual obligations remain pending.
+
 ## SUT Code Generation
 
 The TCK includes a code generator that produces System Under Test (SUT) implementations from Gherkin scenario files in `scenarios/`. The generator supports a `--target` flag to select the SUT type.
